<title>UK: Ecuador sets 2-tranche Eurobond total $500 million.</title>
<headline>Ecuador sets 2-tranche Eurobond total $500 million.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador has set a two-tranche Eurobond for total $500 million, lead manager Chase said on Friday.</p>
<p>The five-year tranche, for $350 million, is a fixed-rate Eurobond to be priced 470 basis points over U.S. Treasury notes.</p>
<p>The seven-year tranche, for $150 million, is a floating rate note to be priced at six-month LIBOR plus 475 b.p.</p>
<p>5-YEAR TRANCHE</p>
<p> AMT    $350 MLN	COUPON     **	  MATURITY    25.APR.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    25.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  70 BP     REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+470 BP</p>
<p> MGT/UND    20 BP     SELL CONC  50 BP     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND FIVE-YEAR U.S TREASURY</p>
<p> NOTES    **TO BE PRICED</p>
<p>* * * *</p>
<p>7-YEAR TRANCHE</p>
<p> AMT    $150 MLN	BASE	 6M-LIBOR  MATURITY	.APR.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN     +475 BP   PAY DATE    25.APR.97</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  =	   ISS PRICE  PAR	 FULL FEES   =</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX/ECUAD DENOMS (K) *	   GOVA LAW    N.Y</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> NOTES	*1K (REGS), 250-1M (144A)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
